a3060c1a-a663-4730-80c7-d9fa8217b675-0
00:27:43.280 --> 00:27:48.202
So Graduate Training for Therapists and
counsellors shares a framework organised

a3060c1a-a663-4730-80c7-d9fa8217b675-1
00:27:48.202 --> 00:27:51.120
around awareness, knowledge,
skills and action.

e7b63eeb-27b8-4ed7-94f7-934c368daaeb-0
00:27:53.200 --> 00:27:59.332
There's also a text that's used
extensively in graduate programs called

e7b63eeb-27b8-4ed7-94f7-934c368daaeb-1
00:27:59.332 --> 00:28:05.890
Counselling the Cultural Diverse by Sue
ET al for accredited counselling and

e7b63eeb-27b8-4ed7-94f7-934c368daaeb-2
00:28:05.890 --> 00:28:11.256
psychology programs,
and it covers awareness of all of our own

e7b63eeb-27b8-4ed7-94f7-934c368daaeb-3
00:28:11.256 --> 00:28:15.600
individual values,
biases and worldview knowledge.

8163c697-9ee0-4c68-b6a5-7919e6f5649c-0
00:28:15.600 --> 00:28:20.175
Having knowledge of diverse client
backgrounds and worldviews,

8163c697-9ee0-4c68-b6a5-7919e6f5649c-1
00:28:20.175 --> 00:28:24.824
skills in culturally responsive
intervention and communication,

8163c697-9ee0-4c68-b6a5-7919e6f5649c-2
00:28:24.824 --> 00:28:30.634
and more recently they added action to
encourage people to actively work toward

8163c697-9ee0-4c68-b6a5-7919e6f5649c-3
00:28:30.634 --> 00:28:32.160
equity and inclusion.

93827fb2-990a-4099-8361-cc4a52dd0aac-0
00:28:32.840 --> 00:28:38.466
So my point with all this is that the
field has already established clear

93827fb2-990a-4099-8361-cc4a52dd0aac-1
00:28:38.466 --> 00:28:42.800
baseline over for for multicultural
competency training.

ef3414da-1528-4522-8b35-42c2c0880ba1-0
00:28:43.200 --> 00:28:47.770
And this can be used by our program and
for people, you know,

ef3414da-1528-4522-8b35-42c2c0880ba1-1
00:28:47.770 --> 00:28:53.520
particularly for people who haven't had
formal training for everyone, really.

cedc5c86-8ad8-4ade-8647-9e82a814879a-0
00:28:57.280 --> 00:29:03.065
Typically multicultural competency covers
race and ethnicity, gender,

cedc5c86-8ad8-4ade-8647-9e82a814879a-1
00:29:03.065 --> 00:29:10.008
socio economic status, sexual orientation,
gender identity, religion, spirituality,

cedc5c86-8ad8-4ade-8647-9e82a814879a-2
00:29:10.008 --> 00:29:14.720
disability, immigration,
language and intersectionality.

ecc11f45-aa30-451d-9ce4-36353ed17beb-0
00:29:15.880 --> 00:29:20.667
And there's a list of what's generally
covered in training,

ecc11f45-aa30-451d-9ce4-36353ed17beb-1
00:29:20.667 --> 00:29:26.491
the cultural humility, bias awareness,
religion and spiritual diversity,

ecc11f45-aa30-451d-9ce4-36353ed17beb-2
00:29:26.491 --> 00:29:30.960
the intersectional everything I just
covered basically.

dfc45037-5f61-401b-b1ac-e9970957ef12-0
00:29:33.760 --> 00:29:38.197
And of course,
psychedelic psychotherapy adds another

dfc45037-5f61-401b-b1ac-e9970957ef12-1
00:29:38.197 --> 00:29:44.361
dimension that requires additional
awareness and training because material

dfc45037-5f61-401b-b1ac-e9970957ef12-2
00:29:44.361 --> 00:29:49.703
surfaces at the height and depth and
speed, as we all well know,

dfc45037-5f61-401b-b1ac-e9970957ef12-3
00:29:49.703 --> 00:29:56.360
and it includes strong emotions, trauma,
and these other heightened sensitivity.

e4dc8d20-036f-465e-937e-c9576ef8f8b0-0
00:29:58.840 --> 00:30:02.958
So the stakes around cultural imposition
are higher than in standard therapy

e4dc8d20-036f-465e-937e-c9576ef8f8b0-1
00:30:02.958 --> 00:30:03.440
sessions.

e624034f-7b34-4edd-a4f4-c1a1ac247faa-0
00:30:03.960 --> 00:30:07.348
So in this context,
multicultural common C isn't just about

e624034f-7b34-4edd-a4f4-c1a1ac247faa-1
00:30:07.348 --> 00:30:08.760
respectful communication.

b5e4276b-5538-4b83-8744-00fbf6f436b1-0
00:30:10.040 --> 00:30:16.795
It includes a sensitivity to world view,
spirituality, language, music, symbolism,

b5e4276b-5538-4b83-8744-00fbf6f436b1-1
00:30:16.795 --> 00:30:19.400
participant autonomy and agency.

6a43ff06-43ba-4855-8f53-23e8db0159cd-0
00:30:21.680 --> 00:30:24.400
So Gregory mentioned Pulitzki ET al,
ET al.

e4853afc-6d4c-4b3b-80ab-139a80c5b38b-0
00:30:24.960 --> 00:30:27.960
He's got a couple of papers I refer to
here.

01955911-c97a-4001-b42e-925474adde12-0
00:30:28.800 --> 00:30:35.008
He's got a comprehensive framework work
for adverse events in psychedelic

01955911-c97a-4001-b42e-925474adde12-1
00:30:35.008 --> 00:30:41.469
psychotherapy that I think we, we,
our group thinks will be very helpful for

01955911-c97a-4001-b42e-925474adde12-2
00:30:41.469 --> 00:30:42.560
this program.

c89416c5-4b69-412d-805a-935db88049a1-0
00:30:43.160 --> 00:30:47.400
He notes the importance of spiritual,
existential,

c89416c5-4b69-412d-805a-935db88049a1-1
00:30:47.400 --> 00:30:52.223
religious and theological dimensions in
psychedelic care,

c89416c5-4b69-412d-805a-935db88049a1-2
00:30:52.223 --> 00:30:58.044
and he has identified a very wide range
of adverse events with direct

c89416c5-4b69-412d-805a-935db88049a1-3
00:30:58.044 --> 00:31:00.040
multicultural relevance.

cf7b5274-bcfc-4a36-9b1d-4da74c64cce2-0
00:31:00.480 --> 00:31:04.705
I'm not going to read them all off,
but a couple that really interested in me

cf7b5274-bcfc-4a36-9b1d-4da74c64cce2-1
00:31:04.705 --> 00:31:05.680
was spiritual one.

d32df664-533a-4753-8ab7-b1087edfb00f-0
00:31:05.680 --> 00:31:12.116
The spiritual and religious injury,
which includes the resurfacing of prior

d32df664-533a-4753-8ab7-b1087edfb00f-1
00:31:12.116 --> 00:31:15.080
religious abuse and Politsky flags.

f9f5a04f-0966-4aa7-9923-f879e918fdf6-0
00:31:15.080 --> 00:31:20.927
This and the therapist facilitate A
tendency to reframe all difficult

f9f5a04f-0966-4aa7-9923-f879e918fdf6-1
00:31:20.927 --> 00:31:26.440
experiences as growth in the in in,
particularly in psychedelics.

24071e5e-f662-42f8-9cba-145cb7d0f159-0
00:31:26.840 --> 00:31:32.520
But he's clear that this can result in
genuine harm going unacknowledged and

24071e5e-f662-42f8-9cba-145cb7d0f159-1
00:31:32.520 --> 00:31:36.800
unaddressed with regard to spiritual or
religious injury.

1c3702d1-ec82-4ff0-8bf7-85c9f69d8e75-0
00:31:38.520 --> 00:31:44.040
He also talks about culturally neutral
therapeutic frames that aren't actually

1c3702d1-ec82-4ff0-8bf7-85c9f69d8e75-1
00:31:44.040 --> 00:31:44.600
neutral.

99fd519a-d14b-4045-bf3f-9f409aeb429c-0
00:31:45.000 --> 00:31:50.086
One that's really interesting is the idea
that therapies present themselves as

99fd519a-d14b-4045-bf3f-9f409aeb429c-1
00:31:50.086 --> 00:31:52.920
culturally neutral when they're not
always.

82141b8a-95b1-410c-84a4-11eeb05ce3c5-0
00:31:53.160 --> 00:31:59.568
Like CBT is shown to have a poor cultural
fit with some Native American populations

82141b8a-95b1-410c-84a4-11eeb05ce3c5-1
00:31:59.568 --> 00:32:03.840
because of its assumptions around the
self rationality.

c116a5a3-5bbb-41b4-b20f-61e421bc0713-0
00:32:04.680 --> 00:32:07.774
You know,
don't believe everything that you think

c116a5a3-5bbb-41b4-b20f-61e421bc0713-1
00:32:07.774 --> 00:32:11.240
and it doesn't always align with other
cultural values.

4d2dec13-c190-4729-90de-50faf88f8caf-0
00:32:13.480 --> 00:32:18.184
So in considering all this,
our recommendations for collecting data

4d2dec13-c190-4729-90de-50faf88f8caf-1
00:32:18.184 --> 00:32:19.360
follow from that.

9c53f45a-0f5b-4103-a745-9dd8f2992140-0
00:32:20.480 --> 00:32:23.877
So first of all,
multicultural competency should be a

9c53f45a-0f5b-4103-a745-9dd8f2992140-1
00:32:23.877 --> 00:32:26.960
certification requirement for everyone
involved.

a4eef681-9ee1-4def-b326-89ae6e3132a3-0
00:32:28.040 --> 00:32:31.092
Second,
participant preferences need to be

a4eef681-9ee1-4def-b326-89ae6e3132a3-1
00:32:31.092 --> 00:32:33.080
assessed during preparation.

88bfdb30-cb2e-4140-b2a5-9f642d04e6ff-0
00:32:33.800 --> 00:32:37.680
Politsky one of the things he says a lot
is we ask rather than assume.

789e8808-5dc9-4753-870f-0b6dfdb7dbdd-0
00:32:38.560 --> 00:32:43.274
That would encompass framing, music,
cultural concerns and prior harmful

789e8808-5dc9-4753-870f-0b6dfdb7dbdd-1
00:32:43.274 --> 00:32:43.920
materials.

33b9ecc3-d40c-40a0-b186-ffa2266b5be4-0
00:32:45.360 --> 00:32:47.880
Third, we need in session protocols.

cd05c355-851e-4d97-bd8d-3e698bb94252-0
00:32:49.360 --> 00:32:50.720
Belle ET al.

f41bb73e-8bcd-471c-96c7-bce1f67100df-0
00:32:50.720 --> 00:32:55.018
Says that training matters,
but that many psychedelic manuals and

f41bb73e-8bcd-471c-96c7-bce1f67100df-1
00:32:55.018 --> 00:33:00.162
practice guidelines still under address
culturally responsive behaviour during

f41bb73e-8bcd-471c-96c7-bce1f67100df-2
00:33:00.162 --> 00:33:01.400
the session itself.

a7b85f00-a6d0-4b4f-8db9-ad5385ce0ba3-0
00:33:03.200 --> 00:33:05.880
4th Therapeutic con Congruence.

84e5557a-857e-4afd-a67b-1198aa47e94a-0
00:33:06.120 --> 00:33:09.883
This is something Gregory's really worked
on a lot,

84e5557a-857e-4afd-a67b-1198aa47e94a-1
00:33:09.883 --> 00:33:15.600
so it's making a good fit between the
client's preferences and the care model.

28b2b01e-fd26-4372-9e2c-a837fcd5efbb-0
00:33:17.640 --> 00:33:22.361
Gregory talks about matching clients to
practitioners where possible,

28b2b01e-fd26-4372-9e2c-a837fcd5efbb-1
00:33:22.361 --> 00:33:26.880
not just matching A modality or
therapeutic approach or framework.

e5ea342d-11f9-4d55-93c8-139898473e71-0
00:33:28.000 --> 00:33:33.112
A client might feel safe with someone who
shares their cultural background or who

e5ea342d-11f9-4d55-93c8-139898473e71-1
00:33:33.112 --> 00:33:37.040
has general cultural knowledge or speaks
their first language.

d79b1262-798e-4906-819b-ba80df256d36-0
00:33:37.680 --> 00:33:41.229
Of course,
perfect match is not always available,

d79b1262-798e-4906-819b-ba80df256d36-1
